  {
    "sha": "043b7e0a962d05e862e72e59cad32aa3fa2df7b1",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDA0M2I3ZTBhOTYyZDA1ZTg2MmU3MmU1OWNhZDMyYWEzZmEyZGY3YjE",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-16T14:50:14Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-16T14:50:14Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(ui): drag rings in Rotate mode turn the selected part\n\nThe viewport bar gets a Rotate button next to Move. With Rotate on, the\none selected part shows three rings round its bounding-box centre, one\nsquare to each shown axis, at a constant 60 px on screen. A drag on a\nring turns the part about that axis through the centre as a preview,\nwith the signed angle above the bar. The release queues one\nTurnModelBy, which runs the existing MoveModel: one undo step, the\ngenerated paths go stale, the stock follows. Escape cancels; a turn\nthat ends at its start adds no step and no rotation noise.\n\nFixes #2047\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
